    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d492">

                <pb facs="0411" n="405" sameAs="frus:frus1939v04/pg405"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">811.51693/112: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of
                            State to the Ambassador in Japan</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Grew</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1939-11-16T18:00:00-05:00">November 16, 1939—6
                        p.m.</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>357. Peiping’s 573, November 8, noon, and 588, November 16, noon, Japanese
                    interference with employees of the National City Bank.<anchor n="82"
                        xml:id="d492-f1"/> Unless you perceive objection or unless the National City
                    Bank at Peiping perceives objection, in which case the Embassy at Peiping is
                    requested to inform you, it is suggested that you take up this matter with the
                    Foreign Office in such manner as you may deem appropriate.<anchor n="83"
                        xml:id="d492-f2"/></p>
                <p>Sent to Tokyo via Peiping. Repeated to Chungking.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Welles</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d492-f1" n="82" xml:id="d492-f1-content">
                <p>Neither printed; they reported details of Japanese pressure placed upon Chinese
                    employees to induce them to reveal information desired (811.51693/110,112).</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d492-f2" n="83" xml:id="d492-f2-content">
                <p>Informal representations were made at Tokyo on December 1.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
